    "dc.description.abstract" : [ {
      "value" : "Summary of The Code on Social Security, 2020\nOverview\n*Title: The Code on Social Security, 2020 *Scope: Consolidates and amends laws to extend social security to all employees and workers in India, including those in unorganized, gig, and platform sectors.\nKey Components\n1. Social Security Governance\n*Boards and Corporations:\n•\tEmployees' Provident Fund Board of Trustees (Central Board): Oversees provident fund schemes.\n•\tEmployees' State Insurance Corporation (Corporation): Manages health and insurance schemes.\n•\tNational and State Social Security Boards: Focus on unorganized workers' welfare.\n•\tState Building Workers' Welfare Boards: Dedicated to building construction workers.\n2. Coverage and Benefits\n*Unorganized, Gig, and Platform Workers:\n•\tMandatory Registration: With conditions (age, self-declaration, Aadhaar).\n•\tSchemes:\n•\tLife, Health, Old Age, Education benefits for unorganized workers.\n•\tSpecific schemes for gig and platform workers, funded by aggregators (1-2% of annual turnover).\n3. Governance and Regulatory Powers\n*Central Government:\n•\tPowers to frame schemes, make rules, and give directions.\n•\tAuthority to exempt aggregators under certain conditions. *State Government:\n•\tPower to make rules consistent with the Code for state-level implementation. *Corporation's Regulatory Powers:\n•\tMake regulations for the administration of its affairs and specified chapters.",
      "language" : null,
      "authority" : null,
      "confidence" : -1,
      "place" : 0
    } ],
